{"tool_name":"hhrep","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"hhrep","home":"https://toolkit.tuebingen.mpg.de/#/tools/hhpred","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Tool for the de novo identification of repeats in protein sequences based on the pairwise comparison of profile hidden Markov models (HMMs).","addition_date":"2017-03-24T11:31:19Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:04:03.596491Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:hhrep","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"mpi-toolkit@tuebingen.mpg.de","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Ab initio structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0476"},{"term":"Repeat sequence detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0379"},{"term":"Sequence comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2451"},{"term":"de Novo sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3644"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"HHrep","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkl130","metadata":{"abstract":"HHrep is a web server for the de novo identification of repeats in protein sequences, which is based on the pairwise comparison of profile hidden Markov models (HMMs). Its main strength is its sensitivity, allowing it to detect highly divergent repeat units in protein sequences whose repeats could as yet only be detected from their structures. Examples include sequences with \u03b2-propellor fold, ferredoxin-like fold, double psi barrels or (\u03b2\u03b1)8 (TIM) barrels. We illustrate this with proteins from four superfamilies of TIM barrels by revealing a clear 4- and 8-fold symmetry, which we detect solely from their sequences. This symmetry might be the trace of an ancient origin through duplication of a \u03b2\u03b1\u03b2\u03b1 or \u03b2\u03b1 unit. HHrep can be accessed at http:// hhrep.tuebingen.mpg.de. \u00a9 The Author 2006. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Biegert A."},{"name":"Remmert M."},{"name":"Soding J."}],"citationCount":66,"date":"2006-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"HHrep: De novo protein repeat detection and the origin of TIM barrels"},"pmcid":"PMC1538828","pmid":"16844977","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein folding, stability and design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0130"},{"term":"Protein folds and structural domains","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736"},{"term":"Sequence composition, complexity and repeats","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0157"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"HHrep","home":"https://bio.tools/hhrep","license":"Unlicense","summary":"Tool for the de novo identification of repeats in protein sequences based on the pairwise comparison of profile hidden Markov models (HMMs).","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:hhrep/web/toolkit.tuebingen.mpg.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"faq":true,"general":true,"help":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":false},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":38,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2017"},{"count":1,"year":"2020"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2006"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2015"},{"count":3,"year":"2008"},{"count":3,"year":"2010"},{"count":3,"year":"2021"},{"count":4,"year":"2009"},{"count":4,"year":"2014"},{"count":6,"year":"2016"}],"doi